1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,085
Welcome to the last lesson of Module 12.

2
00:00:03,085 --> 00:00:07,026
Recurring revenue is the steadiest
money a business can have.

3
00:00:07,026 --> 00:00:12,001
In this lesson, you'll learn to manage
subscriptions, rescue failed payments,

4
00:00:12,001 --> 00:00:14,263
and handle refunds with confidence.

5
00:00:15,113 --> 00:00:17,549
Open Payments, then Subscriptions.

6
00:00:17,549 --> 00:00:20,916
At the top, you can see
4 active subscriptions,

7
00:00:20,916 --> 00:00:25,644
one of them still in its free
trial, bringing in £180 every month.

8
00:00:26,494 --> 00:00:30,377
A subscription starts whenever
someone buys a recurring price,

9
00:00:30,377 --> 00:00:33,697
through a payment link, an
order form, or an invoice.

10
00:00:33,697 --> 00:00:36,140
Their card is saved securely in Stripe,

11
00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:39,146
and charged automatically
on every billing date.

12
00:00:39,997 --> 00:00:41,478
Each one has a status.

13
00:00:41,478 --> 00:00:43,161
Active means it's paying.

14
00:00:43,161 --> 00:00:45,585
Trialing means it's in a free trial.

15
00:00:45,585 --> 00:00:48,210
Past due means the last payment failed.

16
00:00:48,210 --> 00:00:50,432
And cancelled means it has ended.

17
00:00:50,432 --> 00:00:53,394
The buttons above the
list filter by status.

18
00:00:54,244 --> 00:00:57,731
Grace's payment failed,
because her card was declined.

19
00:00:57,731 --> 00:01:00,765
Stripe retries automatically,
but you can help.

20
00:01:00,765 --> 00:01:04,317
Open her subscription, and
click Update payment method.

21
00:01:04,317 --> 00:01:07,480
Kyntlo sends her a secure
link to add a new card.

22
00:01:08,331 --> 00:01:11,604
Ava is moving away, so
let's cancel her smile plan.

23
00:01:11,604 --> 00:01:14,106
Open it, and click Cancel subscription.

24
00:01:14,106 --> 00:01:19,496
Choose to end it at the end of the billing
period, so she keeps what she's paid for.

25
00:01:19,496 --> 00:01:20,331
Then confirm.

26
00:01:21,181 --> 00:01:22,768
Now, Transactions.

27
00:01:22,768 --> 00:01:27,883
This is every payment that has
come in, from every source.

28
00:01:27,883 --> 00:01:31,851
Gross volume is £3,167,
minus £90 of refunds.

29
00:01:31,851 --> 00:01:34,232
And one payment has failed.

30
00:01:35,082 --> 00:01:38,862
Click any payment to see the
details: the card used, the source,

31
00:01:38,862 --> 00:01:43,528
and the Stripe charge ID, which you'll
need if you ever contact Stripe support.

32
00:01:43,528 --> 00:01:46,009
You can resend the receipt from here, too.

33
00:01:46,860 --> 00:01:52,442
Emma’s whitening session was cut short,
so we’ll refund £50 as a goodwill gesture.

34
00:01:52,442 --> 00:01:58,024
Click Refund, choose Partial refund, enter
the amount, pick a reason, and confirm.

35
00:01:58,874 --> 00:02:02,100
The payment is now marked
as partially refunded.

36
00:02:02,100 --> 00:02:07,747
The money goes back to Emma’s card, and
usually arrives within 5 to 10 working days.

37
00:02:07,747 --> 00:02:12,183
Keep in mind that card processing
fees aren’t returned on refunds.

38
00:02:13,032 --> 00:02:16,260
For a full refund, just
leave it set to full refund.

39
00:02:16,260 --> 00:02:20,356
The whole amount goes back, and
the payment is marked as refunded,

40
00:02:20,356 --> 00:02:22,591
like Oliver's check-up payment here.

41
00:02:23,439 --> 00:02:27,725
Further down, Grace's failed payment
shows the reason it was declined.

42
00:02:27,725 --> 00:02:32,622
And when your accountant asks for figures
at the end of the month, click Export,

43
00:02:32,622 --> 00:02:35,500
to download every
transaction as a spreadsheet.

44
00:02:36,351 --> 00:02:37,465
Here's a pro tip.

45
00:02:37,465 --> 00:02:42,771
Every week, filter your subscriptions for
past due, and send each person a short,

46
00:02:42,771 --> 00:02:43,885
friendly message.

47
00:02:43,885 --> 00:02:46,767
Most failed payments
are just expired cards,

48
00:02:46,767 --> 00:02:51,550
and a personal nudge saves far more
of them than automatic retries alone.

49
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:54,038
That's Module 12 complete!

50
00:02:54,038 --> 00:02:57,881
You can now get paid, and manage
every payment that comes in.

51
00:02:57,881 --> 00:03:02,101
In Module 13, we'll create your
first online course in Memberships.

52
00:03:02,101 --> 00:03:02,983
See you there!
